WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.069
Harry Kersh: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:04.604
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:07.073
between Chipotle in the UK and the US.

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:08.408
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:14.114
This is a UK chicken burrito.

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:16.649
We've also got some black
beans, some white rice,

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:20.720
some lettuce, cheese, sour
cream, guac as well inside.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.756
We're gonna measure the length, the–

00:00:22.756 --> 00:00:23.156
[auto-tuned record scratch]

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:24.324
I don't want to say girth.

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:24.858
Producer: You're gonna have to say girth.

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:26.326
I'm gonna make you.
Harry: Aw, man.

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:27.227
Producer: There's going
to be a lot of girth

00:00:27.227 --> 00:00:28.128
in this episode.

00:00:28.762 --> 00:00:29.796
Harry: Game face.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:30.964
We're gonna measure the length,

00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:33.233
the girth, and the weight of this burrito.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.603
So, our burrito is 7 inches long.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.872
Joe Avella: I have the same
burrito Harry has right here.

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:40.607
Well, not the same one. The same order.

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:42.942
I don't know where the burrito
ends and the tinfoil begins,

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:44.611
so I'm kind of eyeballing it.

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:44.778
It looks to be about

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:46.913
It looks to be about

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:49.182
between 7 1/4 and 7 1/2 inches.

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:53.920
Harry: A girth of 10 inches.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.855
[saucy guitar music]

00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:56.923
It has a girth of –

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:58.291
[laughs]

00:00:58.291 --> 00:00:59.826
I promise I'm a professional.

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:01.961
Joe: Its circumference –

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:02.996
girth, really?

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:04.764
Going all the way around.

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:06.232
Almost exactly 10 inches.

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:08.501
Burrito is a 10, if you're

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:10.170
thinking about making it a tux.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:13.473
[upbeat suave music]

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:15.408
Harry: And, finally, it weighs...

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:18.978
more than the scale can handle.

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:21.848
This isn't even the big boy.

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:24.584
Joe: Hey, told you guys
to get a new scale.

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:25.652
We got a new scale.

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:26.753
Harry: Bear with us.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:28.388
[distant screaming]

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:33.860
Harry: So, we're gonna weigh
this burrito half at a time

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.061
to see what the total is.

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:40.233
Half one, 310.

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:41.334
And then this one,

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:43.303
plus I'll get the scraps from the plate.

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:48.875
So, combined, the two halves

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:51.778
of our burrito weighed 597 grams.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:54.747
Joe: Chipotle's burrito order weighed –

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:55.582
man, that's hefty.

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:57.050
That is a hefty boy.

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:01.087
Harry: In the UK, we can
also get our burritos

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:02.088
in bowl form.

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:05.525
This bowl contains the same
ingredients as our burrito,

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:07.060
but obviously without the tortilla wrap.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:09.229
Let's weigh it and see
what it measures up to.

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:12.031
So, this one came out to
pretty much exactly 500 grams,

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.900
which, even with the bowl factored in,

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:16.169
is, like, 100 grams less than the burrito.

00:02:16.436 --> 00:02:19.172
Joe: So, this here is that
same burrito ingredients

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:20.306
in bowl form.

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.543
Whoa, gonna have to go this way.

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:24.911
Oh, wow, I'm really smart.

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:26.613
Wait, is it heavier?

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.915
Wow. So, correct me if I'm wrong,

00:02:28.915 --> 00:02:30.884
but there's more here than
there was in the burrito.

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:34.053
Harry: Finally, we can get our meals

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:35.088
in the form of a salad.

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:37.790
Now, this has all the same
ingredients as our bowl,

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:38.725
but without the rice.

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:40.527
Let's weigh it and see how
much difference that makes.

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:45.265
Strangely enough, this came to pretty much

00:02:45.265 --> 00:02:47.567
exactly 500 grams, the
same as the burrito bowl.

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:51.004
Joe: And here is the salad
version of that bowl,

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:53.173
which was the bowl
version of that burrito.

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:54.941
Sticking with me so far?

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:56.876
Being weighed.

00:02:58.545 --> 00:03:01.047
I do want to point out, this
does have white rice on it.

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:03.216
I mean, salad is boring and disgusting.

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:04.150
I would never get one.

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:05.752
Harry: In the UK, you
can only get one size

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:07.320
of chips on the side,

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.589
and that's roughly this many.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.125
Some of these are a little bit fractured,

00:03:12.125 --> 00:03:14.661
so I will just try and form
whole chips where I can.

00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:17.931
I'm like the Banksy of tortilla chips.

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:19.465
Banksy, you've done it again.

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:22.035
29, 30, and a half.

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:25.505
Joe: At a US Chipotle, you
have two sizes of chips,

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:27.006
the regular

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:29.008
and the large.

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:31.611
Regular chips first.

00:03:31.611 --> 00:03:32.979
That's gonna take forever.

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:34.380
All right, one.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.715
[fast-forwarding]

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:38.685
25, 30, 35, some broken ones.

00:03:38.685 --> 00:03:41.187
[normal speed] A regular
bag is roughly 41 chips.

00:03:41.187 --> 00:03:42.288
Now let's count the large.

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:49.062
75, 76.

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:52.765
Nearly double for the large
bag of chips at Chipotle.

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:53.433
Very nice.

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:54.934
Harry: In the UK, we can only get

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:56.636
one size of guac on the side.

00:03:56.636 --> 00:03:58.071
It's supposed to be 4 ounces.

00:03:58.071 --> 00:03:59.739
We're gonna measure it to
check if that's the case.

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:04.377
Ours was just shy of 4 ounces,

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:05.778
so pretty much right.

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:07.113
Joe: The guac in the US,

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:09.782
of course, comes in two sizes as well,

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:11.651
and I'm gonna weigh
them just to make sure.

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:12.752
Just to keep them honest.

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:14.687
I don't know how much
the measuring cup is.

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:16.856
So it should be over
4 ounces, if anything.

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:19.759
3.75.

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:20.593
[clears throat]

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:21.828
That's including the cup,

00:04:21.828 --> 00:04:24.030
which, correct me if I'm
wrong, you do not eat.

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:27.000
Skimping on the guac.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:30.036
Don't act like 0.25
ounces isn't that much.

00:04:30.036 --> 00:04:32.005
If it's not that much,
then put it in there.

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:34.874
8 o-zeezers.

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:37.677
It's a little over 7.

00:04:37.744 --> 00:04:39.946
Zoom in on that. I want
to shame these people.

00:04:39.946 --> 00:04:41.447
Shame on you, Chipotle.

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:42.915
You already charged us extra for it,

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:44.217
and you're also just not giving us

00:04:44.217 --> 00:04:45.418
as much as we pay for.

00:04:45.418 --> 00:04:46.185
Tsk,

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:46.719
tsk!

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:48.454
Harry: And, finally, we have tacos.

00:04:48.855 --> 00:04:49.689
Oh, hell, yeah.

00:04:50.256 --> 00:04:51.858
When we looked at the menu,
they were only available

00:04:51.858 --> 00:04:53.493
in a portion size of three.

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:56.029
In the UK, this taco
is 6 inches in length.

00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:57.463
We got a veggie taco,

00:04:57.463 --> 00:05:00.800
which includes guac, salsa, sour cream,

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:04.037
cheese, fajita vegetables,
and black beans.

00:05:04.037 --> 00:05:05.204
And ours weighs....

00:05:07.407 --> 00:05:08.408
Joe: At a US Chipotle,

00:05:08.408 --> 00:05:11.711
you can get tacos in orders
of one, two, or three.

00:05:11.711 --> 00:05:13.646
This guy's falling apart.

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:14.681
It's a 6-incher.

00:05:14.681 --> 00:05:16.816
And, of course,

00:05:16.816 --> 00:05:20.787
I did not get a vegetarian taco.

00:05:20.787 --> 00:05:22.755
This one has meats aplenty.

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:24.090
So it has different ingredients

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:25.325
than the one that they weighed,

00:05:25.325 --> 00:05:29.128
making this weighing completely arbitrary!

00:05:30.163 --> 00:05:31.297
Harry: Now, this [burrito thuds]

00:05:31.297 --> 00:05:33.666
is the biggest burrito you
can get at a UK Chipotle.

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:34.701
We chose chicken as the base,

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:37.036
but then we added every
other meat as an add-on,

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:39.572
and we've also got all the
vegetables and all the salsas.

00:05:39.572 --> 00:05:40.940
They were a bit reluctant to make this,

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:42.342
but eventually they got it done,

00:05:42.342 --> 00:05:43.376
and it seems to not be leaking,

00:05:43.376 --> 00:05:44.377
so good job, guys.

00:05:44.577 --> 00:05:47.046
Joe: This right here is the
biggest burrito you can get

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:48.548
at a Chipotle in the US.

00:05:48.548 --> 00:05:51.617
So big, in fact, I named it the Big Boy.

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:52.452
Got that?

00:05:52.452 --> 00:05:53.186
Fantastic.

00:05:53.186 --> 00:05:54.320
OK, "What's in it?" you ask.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:56.956
Well, it's a carnitas
burrito with double carnitas,

00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:58.958
and I also got double barbacoa.

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:00.026
Of course it's double wrapped,

00:06:00.026 --> 00:06:04.497
because it has guacamole,
white rice, fajita veggies,

00:06:04.497 --> 00:06:07.834
black beans, queso blanco, mild tomato,

00:06:07.834 --> 00:06:09.902
I actually got all the salsas,

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:12.538
sour cream, cheese, and lettuce.

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:16.376
This runs about $18.20 in the US,

00:06:16.376 --> 00:06:20.646
which is about 13 pounds and 16 shillings.

00:06:20.646 --> 00:06:23.182
Harry: This burrito set
me back 16 pounds 75,

00:06:23.182 --> 00:06:25.985
which is around $22,
which is quite expensive.

00:06:25.985 --> 00:06:28.888
You're looking at kind of 2
pounds 70 per meat you add in,

00:06:28.888 --> 00:06:31.157
so, honestly, if you're looking
for just quantity for lunch,

00:06:31.157 --> 00:06:33.526
it's probably cheaper to
just get two single burritos.

00:06:33.526 --> 00:06:35.061
Now, it's the same length
as the other burrito,

00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:36.229
coming in at 7 inches,

00:06:36.229 --> 00:06:38.498
but you do get one extra inch of girth.

00:06:38.498 --> 00:06:40.533
And, as we all know, a little goes –

00:06:40.533 --> 00:06:41.200
[laughs]

00:06:41.534 --> 00:06:44.537
As we all know, a little goes a long way.

00:06:44.537 --> 00:06:45.738
[laughs]

00:06:45.905 --> 00:06:49.175
Joe: Now I will measure the length

00:06:49.175 --> 00:06:52.011
and thickness of this one.

00:06:52.078 --> 00:06:53.479
Almost 9 inches.

00:06:53.479 --> 00:06:57.717
OK, it's about 8 3/4.

00:06:57.717 --> 00:07:00.620
Yo, this guy's a lot thicker.

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:03.723
So, that's about 11 1/2
inches of thickness.

00:07:03.723 --> 00:07:04.690
It's much bigger.

00:07:07.727 --> 00:07:08.895
Harry: What about the calories?

00:07:08.895 --> 00:07:11.097
Well, this is the most
popular burrito from Chipotle.

00:07:11.097 --> 00:07:12.465
It contains eight ingredients:

00:07:12.465 --> 00:07:15.902
chicken, white rice,
black beans, sour cream,

00:07:15.902 --> 00:07:19.505
guacamole, cheese, fresh
tomato salsa, and lettuce.

00:07:19.505 --> 00:07:21.908
This contains 1,320 calories,

00:07:21.908 --> 00:07:23.810
540 of which are from fat.

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:26.779
It does contain 2,610 milligrams of sodium,

00:07:26.779 --> 00:07:29.348
which is 113% of your daily allowance.

00:07:29.615 --> 00:07:31.751
Joe: And in the US, that same burrito,

00:07:31.751 --> 00:07:34.320
according to Chipotle, is the exact same nutrition

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:35.288
and calorie count.

00:07:35.288 --> 00:07:37.356
They use the same smallwares and utensils

00:07:37.356 --> 00:07:39.692
to make the burritos in the
UK as they do in the US,

00:07:39.692 --> 00:07:41.828
so everything should
technically be the same.

00:07:41.828 --> 00:07:43.529
That's what their PR people told us.

00:07:43.529 --> 00:07:45.031
And, hey, if you can't trust

00:07:45.031 --> 00:07:46.766
a major conglomerate's PR people,

00:07:46.766 --> 00:07:48.167
who can you trust, right?

00:07:48.167 --> 00:07:50.470
And if you get that
same order in salad form

00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:53.039
and didn't put rice on
your salad like a maniac,

00:07:53.039 --> 00:07:55.908
that would bring this calorie
count down to about 800,

00:07:55.908 --> 00:07:59.712
and it lowers the sodium
to "only" 1,520 milligrams,

00:07:59.712 --> 00:08:02.615
or 66% of what you should have in the day.

00:08:02.782 --> 00:08:04.217
Chipotle also gives you the option

00:08:04.217 --> 00:08:07.153
of having their vinaigrette
salad dressing on the side,

00:08:07.153 --> 00:08:09.322
which adds 220 calories,

00:08:09.322 --> 00:08:12.825
bumping it back up over
1,000 to 1,020 calories

00:08:12.825 --> 00:08:17.697
and bumping up the sodium
to 2,327 milligrams,

00:08:17.697 --> 00:08:20.132
or 101% of your daily –

00:08:20.132 --> 00:08:21.868
basically, it's liquid salt.

00:08:22.301 --> 00:08:23.803
What's with the...? Jeez.

00:08:24.003 --> 00:08:25.805
Harry: If you choose to get
your burrito in a bowl form,

00:08:25.805 --> 00:08:27.607
that loses you 320 calories,

00:08:27.607 --> 00:08:29.509
bringing it down to an even 1,000.

00:08:29.509 --> 00:08:32.311
Now it's only around 40% of
your daily caloric allowance.

00:08:32.311 --> 00:08:36.415
It still contains 1,855
milligrams of sodium, however.

00:08:36.782 --> 00:08:39.952
In the UK, a side of
chips is 540 calories.

00:08:39.952 --> 00:08:41.420
Joe: Same with our regular chips here.

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:42.955
Now, if you upgrade to the large,

00:08:42.955 --> 00:08:45.291
that's going to be 810 calories.

00:08:45.391 --> 00:08:47.426
Harry: If you were to enjoy
these with a side of guac,

00:08:47.426 --> 00:08:49.295
that's an extra 230 calories.

00:08:49.295 --> 00:08:51.697
Joe: Now, if you wanted to
upgrade to the large guac,

00:08:51.697 --> 00:08:54.467
that's gonna be an
additional 460 calories.

00:08:56.903 --> 00:08:58.538
Harry: Now, Chipotle as
a brand prides themself

00:08:58.538 --> 00:08:59.872
on being quite a healthy option.

00:08:59.872 --> 00:09:02.108
They're not using too many
artificial ingredients.

00:09:02.108 --> 00:09:03.509
In the US, they actually make a big deal

00:09:03.509 --> 00:09:06.746
of only needing 53 ingredients
across the entire menu.

00:09:06.746 --> 00:09:08.281
However, in the UK, when we totaled up

00:09:08.281 --> 00:09:10.550
all of the ingredients, we found 67.

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:12.218
So, as you all know if
you watch "Food Wars,"

00:09:12.218 --> 00:09:13.586
that's kind of unusual
that there's more things

00:09:13.586 --> 00:09:14.887
in the US than in the UK.

00:09:14.987 --> 00:09:17.690
Joe: The only ingredient
in the US Chipotle

00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:20.593
that gave me a bit of pause
was something called gypsum.

00:09:20.593 --> 00:09:24.163
Gypsum's also known as calcium
sulfate [di]hydrate, right?

00:09:24.163 --> 00:09:27.133
OK, and Chipotle uses
that in their tofu process

00:09:27.133 --> 00:09:28.801
when they separate the
chunks from the liquid.

00:09:28.801 --> 00:09:31.971
Gypsum is also found in
drywall, chalk, and shampoo.

00:09:31.971 --> 00:09:32.838
Of course it is.

00:09:32.838 --> 00:09:35.207
Now, does the gypsum stay in the tofu,

00:09:35.207 --> 00:09:38.177
or is it just used for
the separating purposes?

00:09:38.177 --> 00:09:39.011
I don't care.

00:09:39.011 --> 00:09:40.746
I'm never getting tofu from Chipotle.

00:09:42.148 --> 00:09:44.116
Harry: Put the beast back in front of me.

00:09:44.483 --> 00:09:46.686
Let's look at some ingredients
for the flour tortillas.

00:09:46.686 --> 00:09:49.255
In the UK, the tortillas
contain fortified wheat flour

00:09:49.255 --> 00:09:51.757
(wheat flour, calcium carbonate, iron,

00:09:51.757 --> 00:09:53.960
niacin, thiamine, water,

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:56.028
vegetable oils (palm oil, rapeseed oil),

00:09:56.028 --> 00:09:58.464
wholemeal flour, salt, and raising agents

00:09:58.464 --> 00:10:01.133
(sodium carbonate,
diphosphates, and malic acid).

00:10:01.133 --> 00:10:01.968
Joe: In the US,

00:10:01.968 --> 00:10:04.236
our flour tortilla only
has four ingredients.

00:10:04.236 --> 00:10:06.973
Wheat flour, water, canola oil, and salt.

00:10:06.973 --> 00:10:07.707
That's it.

00:10:08.441 --> 00:10:09.041
Huh.

00:10:09.809 --> 00:10:11.243
Harry: Now I know how
Joe feels when we film

00:10:11.243 --> 00:10:12.478
pretty much all of these episodes,

00:10:12.478 --> 00:10:13.546
because it's not very nice

00:10:13.546 --> 00:10:15.047
to have that many things in your food

00:10:15.047 --> 00:10:16.282
knowing that the other side doesn't.

00:10:16.282 --> 00:10:17.917
Like, why do we need it but they don't?

00:10:17.917 --> 00:10:18.517
It's weird.

00:10:18.718 --> 00:10:20.186
Now, given the fact that we
have way more ingredients

00:10:20.186 --> 00:10:21.520
in the UK than in the US,

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:23.289
it does beg the question
as to why the calorie count

00:10:23.289 --> 00:10:25.024
for their tortillas is the same.

00:10:25.024 --> 00:10:27.126
We did reach out to
Chipotle for explanation,

00:10:27.126 --> 00:10:28.394
but unfortunately at
the time of recording,

00:10:28.394 --> 00:10:29.595
they hadn't got back to us.

00:10:29.695 --> 00:10:30.630
Besides the tortillas,

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:32.064
a lot of the other fillings at Chipotle

00:10:32.064 --> 00:10:33.466
have pretty similar ingredients lists

00:10:33.466 --> 00:10:34.800
in the UK and the US,

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:37.103
maybe with some minor
differences in the spices used.

00:10:37.103 --> 00:10:39.372
For example, the chicken
in the UK is flavored

00:10:39.372 --> 00:10:42.875
with chicken, water, chile
de árbol and jalapeño,

00:10:42.875 --> 00:10:45.511
cumin, garlic, oregano, black pepper,

00:10:45.511 --> 00:10:47.346
sea salt, and sunflower oil.

00:10:47.346 --> 00:10:49.715
Joe: Whereas our chicken
is chicken, obviously,

00:10:49.715 --> 00:10:51.784
water, chipotle chili, cumin,

00:10:51.784 --> 00:10:54.320
garlic, oregano, black pepper, salt,

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:56.856
distilled vinegar, and sunflower oil.

00:10:56.856 --> 00:10:59.191
All words I can pronounce! Huzzah!

00:10:59.358 --> 00:11:00.526
Harry: Our guacamole is pretty simple.

00:11:00.526 --> 00:11:02.328
It only has six ingredients.

00:11:02.328 --> 00:11:04.397
Avocado, red onion, jalapeño,

00:11:04.397 --> 00:11:06.832
citrus juice, sea-salt
flakes, and coriander,

00:11:06.832 --> 00:11:08.768
which is what we call cilantro,

00:11:08.768 --> 00:11:09.669
and we're definitely right.

00:11:09.835 --> 00:11:11.237
Joe: US guac is very similar.

00:11:11.237 --> 00:11:14.507
Avocado, cilantro or coriander,
whatever it's called,

00:11:14.507 --> 00:11:18.344
jalapeños, lemon juice, lime
juice, onions, and salt.

00:11:18.411 --> 00:11:19.512
Harry: A serving of white rice

00:11:19.512 --> 00:11:22.448
in the UK is made of
long-grain white rice,

00:11:22.448 --> 00:11:24.583
bay leaf, sunflower oil, coriander,

00:11:24.583 --> 00:11:26.252
citrus juice, and sea-salt flakes.

00:11:26.285 --> 00:11:29.388
Joe: And our white rice in
the US contains white rice,

00:11:29.388 --> 00:11:32.525
bay leaf, cilantro,
lemon juice, lime juice,

00:11:32.525 --> 00:11:36.162
rice-bran oil, salt, and water.

00:11:36.395 --> 00:11:39.131
Harry: Finally, our Monterey
Jack cheese contains milk,

00:11:39.131 --> 00:11:42.201
starter cheese culture,
sea-salt flakes, and enzymes.

00:11:42.201 --> 00:11:44.103
Don't know which enzymes. Just enzymes.

00:11:44.103 --> 00:11:45.237
The concept of enzymes.

00:11:45.237 --> 00:11:47.606
Joe: Whereas our cheese
contains cheese curds,

00:11:47.606 --> 00:11:49.041
nope. Cheese cultures,

00:11:49.041 --> 00:11:52.378
milk, salt, and vegetable rennet.

00:11:52.378 --> 00:11:53.479
Rennet?

00:11:53.479 --> 00:11:54.580
Ren-net.

00:11:54.580 --> 00:11:56.048
I don't know what that is.

00:11:58.484 --> 00:11:59.685
Harry: Here is everything
you will only find

00:11:59.685 --> 00:12:01.187
on the menu at a UK Chipotle.

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:04.490
Joe: These are all the
US-exclusive items at Chipotle.

00:12:04.590 --> 00:12:06.525
Harry: Now, we only have
one exclusive food item

00:12:06.525 --> 00:12:07.393
on the menu in the UK,

00:12:07.393 --> 00:12:09.729
and that is the protein pump bowl.

00:12:09.729 --> 00:12:12.498
It contains rice, a
double order of chicken,

00:12:12.498 --> 00:12:15.234
some lettuce, some salsa, and some cheese.

00:12:15.568 --> 00:12:17.369
Joe: This first one right
here is the whole 30 bowl,

00:12:17.369 --> 00:12:19.171
for those of you on the whole 30 diet.

00:12:19.271 --> 00:12:20.406
In the middle...

00:12:20.406 --> 00:12:21.440
cheat sheet No. 2,

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:22.942
this is the paleo bowl,

00:12:22.942 --> 00:12:26.112
and that is a chicken
salad with guacamole,

00:12:26.112 --> 00:12:28.080
lettuce, fajita veggies, chicken,

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:29.815
and the medium green salsa.

00:12:30.082 --> 00:12:33.152
And the last bowl over here
is the protein pump bowl.

00:12:33.152 --> 00:12:34.286
It's got all that stuff in it.

00:12:34.487 --> 00:12:38.591
This right here is
Chipotle's queso cheese.

00:12:38.591 --> 00:12:40.493
Not available in the UK.

00:12:40.593 --> 00:12:41.827
What is the story with this?

00:12:41.861 --> 00:12:44.797
They figured out a way to
make natural melted cheese,

00:12:44.797 --> 00:12:45.664
and I gotta tell you,

00:12:45.664 --> 00:12:48.567
this stuff is really good.

00:12:48.768 --> 00:12:50.202
[crunching]

00:12:50.202 --> 00:12:51.470
Yeah. Oh, man.

00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:52.738
Like, their queso is trouble.

00:12:52.738 --> 00:12:53.706
I love that stuff.

00:12:53.706 --> 00:12:54.540
It's really good.

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:56.909
A protein that you can get
in the US is carne asada.

00:12:56.909 --> 00:12:58.611
You can get that instead of the steak.

00:12:58.611 --> 00:12:59.779
And cauliflower rice.

00:12:59.779 --> 00:13:02.681
Now, there was no
cauliflower rice available

00:13:02.681 --> 00:13:04.550
at the Chipotles we
went to for this video,

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:06.218
but besides that, I went ahead

00:13:06.218 --> 00:13:10.856
and made a US Only Chipotle taco.

00:13:10.856 --> 00:13:13.025
It's just a queso and carne asada taco.

00:13:13.025 --> 00:13:14.593
I figured a burrito

00:13:14.593 --> 00:13:17.863
of just carne asada and
queso is a little ridiculous.

00:13:17.863 --> 00:13:19.031
This is like what I would have gotten

00:13:19.031 --> 00:13:20.800
when I was in the seventh grade as a kid,

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:23.135
just melted cheese and
meat and nothing else.

00:13:23.135 --> 00:13:23.969
So, here we go.

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:29.275
Yeah.

00:13:29.275 --> 00:13:30.476
[mumbles]

00:13:30.476 --> 00:13:32.311
[upbeat jazzy music]

00:13:32.311 --> 00:13:33.779
I love the queso. It's incredible.

00:13:33.779 --> 00:13:35.748
Carne asada's really good.

00:13:35.748 --> 00:13:37.917
Chipotle also has a children's menu.

00:13:37.917 --> 00:13:39.985
You can get two tacos or quesadillas.

00:13:39.985 --> 00:13:41.187
I was surprised to learn

00:13:41.187 --> 00:13:43.022
with the tacos for the kids' meal,

00:13:43.022 --> 00:13:45.457
you get one meat and two toppings.

00:13:45.558 --> 00:13:47.359
Yes, kids are picky eaters.

00:13:47.359 --> 00:13:49.295
But only two toppings, mom and dad?

00:13:49.295 --> 00:13:50.362
Only two?

00:13:50.529 --> 00:13:51.497
Also, it comes with your choice

00:13:51.497 --> 00:13:54.667
of chocolate milk or apple juice.

00:13:54.934 --> 00:13:56.635
Harry: What we lack in
exclusive food options

00:13:56.635 --> 00:13:57.603
and in fountain drinks

00:13:57.603 --> 00:14:00.606
we really make up for in
cans and bottles of drink.

00:14:00.639 --> 00:14:01.974
So, let's start with
these things over here,

00:14:01.974 --> 00:14:05.277
which are Tenzing brand
natural energy drinks.

00:14:05.277 --> 00:14:08.247
It's kind of like when you
want a Red Bull slash coffee,

00:14:08.247 --> 00:14:10.482
but you don't want the
guilt associated with it.

00:14:10.482 --> 00:14:12.952
Then we have this very
fancily named Fentimans,

00:14:12.952 --> 00:14:14.753
which is kind of like a sparkling water

00:14:14.753 --> 00:14:16.055
flavored with elderflower.

00:14:16.055 --> 00:14:17.656
Personally, not a huge fan of elderflower,

00:14:17.656 --> 00:14:19.558
but some people are, and that's OK.

00:14:19.558 --> 00:14:22.928
Next, we have this
Turmeric and Mango Nourish

00:14:22.928 --> 00:14:24.496
from Humble Warrior.

00:14:24.496 --> 00:14:27.266
Next up, we've got these
cans of Dash Water,

00:14:27.266 --> 00:14:29.068
which, I think they're just water

00:14:29.068 --> 00:14:30.669
that's kind of lightly flavored again.

00:14:30.669 --> 00:14:31.704
We have orange juice,

00:14:31.704 --> 00:14:34.006
we have Berry Set Go,

00:14:34.006 --> 00:14:35.241
and we have Wonder Green,

00:14:35.241 --> 00:14:36.909
if you want something nice and healthy.

00:14:36.909 --> 00:14:38.644
Chipotle's kind of gone for a fancier vibe

00:14:38.644 --> 00:14:39.745
with these, by the looks of things.

00:14:39.745 --> 00:14:41.947
These are all kind of the fancier brands.

00:14:41.947 --> 00:14:43.616
At the end of the day, they
are kind of just sodas,

00:14:43.616 --> 00:14:45.317
but they're ones that are
just a bit more upmarket

00:14:45.317 --> 00:14:46.285
than you might normally find.

00:14:46.285 --> 00:14:47.620
A personal highlight is that Chipotle

00:14:47.620 --> 00:14:49.355
in the UK sells San Pellegrino.

00:14:49.355 --> 00:14:50.556
I don't know if you guys
have this in the US,

00:14:50.556 --> 00:14:53.692
but it's basically a brand
of sparkling fruit juices.

00:14:53.692 --> 00:14:54.960
I really love their lemonade.

00:14:54.960 --> 00:14:56.428
It's, like, really tangy and acidic.

00:14:56.629 --> 00:14:57.997
And then, finally, if you want to,

00:14:57.997 --> 00:14:59.665
you can finish off your meal with a beer.

00:14:59.865 --> 00:15:00.866
Joe: Looks like the ones over there

00:15:00.866 --> 00:15:02.601
in the UK are pretty much different

00:15:02.601 --> 00:15:04.136
than the ones we have in the US,

00:15:04.136 --> 00:15:05.671
and this is not even all of them.

00:15:05.671 --> 00:15:08.007
I have the Nantucket Nectars,

00:15:08.007 --> 00:15:09.108
which is juice.

00:15:09.108 --> 00:15:11.410
I see these are Iz? Izze?

00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:14.146
You guys had the cans of
the San Pellegrino water.

00:15:14.146 --> 00:15:16.482
We just have the bottle of the plain,

00:15:16.482 --> 00:15:17.816
which I actually prefer.

00:15:17.950 --> 00:15:20.052
Yo. Organic black tea.

00:15:20.052 --> 00:15:22.021
And right here,

00:15:22.021 --> 00:15:23.122
the best one,

00:15:24.189 --> 00:15:25.024
Mexican Coke.

00:15:25.024 --> 00:15:26.792
Harry: It really sucks
that America is so obsessed

00:15:26.792 --> 00:15:27.893
with high-fructose corn syrup,

00:15:27.893 --> 00:15:29.194
because our Coke I think is similar

00:15:29.194 --> 00:15:31.897
to Mexican Coke and just
made with regular sugar.

00:15:31.897 --> 00:15:33.232
Would you like a tortilla chip

00:15:33.232 --> 00:15:35.301
having been loosely fondled by me?

